      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty has emerged as a mode of treatment in patients with both chronic and acute coronary syndromes. Among the recognized complications of coronary angioplasty is coronary embolism. This case report describes a case of acute anterior myocardial infarction which was treated with angioplasty of the left anterior descending coronary artery. Postdilation angiography revealed obstruction of the posterior descending artery (in a left dominant system). The use of thrombolytic therapy previous to angioplasty is briefly discussed."},
